    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="56">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 56</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif open morð weorðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.19"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man sy amyrred<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.20"/>, agyfe man þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.13"/> magum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>Open morð. Gyf open morð weorðe, ðæt man amyrred sy, agyue man magum [þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.4"/> banan].</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif open morð weorðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man sy amyrdred<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.2"/>, agife man þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.3"/> magum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui murdrum aperte perpetrabit, reddatur parentibus interfecti.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Si apertum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.11"/> mordrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.12"/> fuerit, ut aliquis per illud<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_56.lnote.oe.13-2"/> occidatur, reddatur parentibus suis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="56" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>[56] Si mortificat[ur]a manifesta fuerit, malefactor cognatis tradatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="56" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="202" ed="#robertson"/>Open morð. Gif open morð weorðe ðæt man amyrred<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_56.robnote.fn.11"/> sy, agyue man magum<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_56.robnote.fn.12"/> [þone banan]<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_56.robnote.fn.10"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif open morð weorðe þæt man sy amyrðred, agyfe man þam magum þone banan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_56.lnote.de.1"/> ein unleugbarer heimlicher Mord<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_56.lnote.de.2"/> geschieht, so dass ein Mensch vernichtet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_56.lnote.de.3"/> (ermordet <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) ist, so liefere man an die Verwandten [des Getödteten] (den<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_56.lnote.de.4"/> Mörder <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) aus.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If an undeniable secret murder happens, so that a person is destroyed (murdered, A), let [the killer] (the murderer, B) be handed over to the kinsmen [of the slain].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="203" ed="#robertson"/>Murder which is discovered. If anyone dies by violence and it becomes evident that it is a case of murder<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_56.robnote.n.1"/>, the murderer shall be given up to the kinsmen [of the slain man].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>If manifest murder occur,<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_56.whinote.n.2"/> so that a man is destroyed, [the murderer] is to be given up to the kinsmen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="285" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If it comes to be shown that someone who has died violently has been murdered, the murderer shall be surrendered to the family of the victim.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 349, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Open morð</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">amyrðred: amyrred G</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þone banan: omitted GA, added in B in a sixteenth-century hand</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cata <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cata Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[<hi rend="italic">eingeklammertes</hi>] <hi rend="italic">am Rande im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[the bracketed words] in the margin in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">amyrdrede, agife <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">amyrdrede, agife Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðara <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðara Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> amyrðred <hi rend="italic">wie</hi> 24, 2 drywa; 50, 1 bid</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read amyrðred, as at 24, 2 drywa; 50, 1 bid</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> þam</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read þam</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quis a. m. fecerit <hi rend="italic">LbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quis a. m. fecerit LbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so HDi;</hi> mur. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus HDi; mur. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">illum <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">illum S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ergänze in Übs. als Überschrift: ‘Unleugbarer Mord <hi rend="italic">B</hi>.’—Dreimal benutzt den Satz Hn 71, 1. 91, 15; 18 mit Erklärung, dass, im Ggs. zu <hi rend="italic">compellatio</hi>, ‘offenbar’ bei <hi rend="italic">homicidium</hi> bedeute: Delinquent sei <hi rend="italic">confessus vel convictus. Vgl. o</hi>. 53¹; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> bandhaft 1f. g. 4. 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the translation add as heading: ‘Undeniable murder <hi rend="italic">B</hi>.’—Hn uses the sentence three times, 71, 1. 91, 15; 18, with the explanation that, in contrast to <hi rend="italic">compellatio</hi>, ‘manifest’ with <hi rend="italic">homicidium</hi> means: the delinquent is <hi rend="italic">confessus vel convictus. Cf. above</hi> 53¹; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> bandhaft 1f. g. 4. 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Mord 2c. 5. 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Mord 2c. 5. 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">amyrdrian</hi> setzt Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. an; Sweet: <hi rend="italic">amyrðrian</hi>. Für <hi rend="italic">amirran</hi> steht die Bed. <hi rend="italic">perdere</hi> auch von Menschenleben fest</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>. sets up <hi rend="italic">amyrdrian</hi>; Sweet: <hi rend="italic">amyrðrian</hi>. For <hi rend="italic">amirran</hi> the meaning <hi rend="italic">perdere</hi> is established also of human life</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_56.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B's Ergänzung ist sinngemäss, aber nicht aus Archetyp. Dieser hatte vielleicht als Objekt, das kaum fehlen kann, ·<hi rend="italic">N</hi>· d. h. <hi rend="italic">hine</hi>, was die drei Übersetzer, aber nicht die Abschreiber verstanden, wie A <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 45, 3; oder diese übersahen es.—Auslieferer ist das Gericht, nicht die Sippe (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 17a) des Mörders; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Preisgebung</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B's addition accords with the sense, but is not from the archetype. This perhaps had as object, which can scarcely be missing, ·<hi rend="italic">N</hi>·, i.e. <hi rend="italic">hine</hi>, which the three translators understood but the copyists did not, like A <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 45, 3; or else the copyists overlooked it.—The one who hands over is the court, not the kindred (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 17a) of the murderer; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Preisgebung</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_56.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This clause seems tautological. For a parallel translation to the one I have given, see BT. p. 698, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">morð</hi>, <hi rend="smallcaps">iii</hi>. For another version see BT. p. 763, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">open</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_56.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>of</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Written in the margin in 16th cent. in B; om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_56.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>amyrred</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">amyrdred</hi> (<hi rend="italic">-drede</hi>) A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_56.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>magum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þam</hi> (<hi rend="italic">þara, ðara</hi>), <hi rend="italic">m.</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_56.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">470</biblScope></bibl><label>occur</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Murder to the Anglo-Saxons meant killing by secret means.</seg></note>
      </div>
